{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sequential and simultaneous multiphysics solutions sequential and simultaneous multiphysics solutions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions.md","fileName":"Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","Nonisothermal Flow","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sequential and simultaneous multiphysics solutions sequential and simultaneous multiphysics solutions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions.md","fileName":"Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions","heading":"Sequential and Simultaneous Multiphysics Solutions","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"In a sequential multiphysics solution, one physics is solved first and its field is passed as input to another. This can reduce the size of each solve and is appropriate when feedback from the later physics to the earlier one is negligible.\n\nA simultaneous solution assembles interdependent fields so they converge together. It is needed when fluid motion c